To add this MCP to the Claude Desktop app, edit your config file:

**1. Open the config file:**
- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`

**2. Add this to the file:**

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "onchainchess": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/Users/gold/VS code/claude/chess UI/mcp/index.js"],
      "env": {
        "CHESS_SERVER_URL": "https://onchainchess-production.up.railway.app"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

If the file already has other MCP servers, just add the `"onchainchess": { ... }` block inside the existing `"mcpServers"` object.

**3. Make sure dependencies are installed:**
```
cd "/Users/gold/VS code/claude/chess UI/mcp" && npm install
```

**4. Restart Claude Desktop** — the chess tools should appear in the toolbox (hammer icon).

Set `CHESS_SERVER_URL` to `http://localhost:3001` if you want to play against a local server instead of production.
